# Practicing a spell from a guildmaster teaches the player, even when the
# player's mirror images stand ahead of them in the room. The images are named
# after the player, so a lookup by name used to hand the lesson to an image
# and the player's scribing never started.
staff  Imagestaff
actor  Conjo class=CONJURER level=30 skill=SKILL_SCRIBE:100 skill=SPELL_MIRROR_IMAGE:100

Imagestaff> trans Conjo
until Imagestaff /architect/ max 3 load mob 64
until Imagestaff /master spellbook/ max 3 load obj 7
Imagestaff> give master Conjo
Conjo> rest
Conjo> memorize mirror image
until Conjo /finished memorizing/ max 60 memorize
Conjo> drop master
Conjo? You drop
until Imagestaff /a spellbook/ max 3 load obj 203
until Imagestaff /quill/ max 3 load obj 204
Imagestaff> give spellbook Conjo
Imagestaff> give quill Conjo
Conjo> stand
until Conjo /spitting image/ max 5 cast 'mirror image'
# Moving an image puts it at the head of the room, ahead of Conjo.
Imagestaff> trans image
Conjo> hold spellbook
Conjo> hold quill
Conjo? You hold a quill
Conjo> rest

Conjo> practice feeblemind
Conjo? (?s)The architect starts to teach you feeblemind.*You finish scribing the spell 'feeblemind'
